course: dictionary
lesson: 11839
title: Words that stand in for others
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sometimes people do not want to say a rude word, so they pick a milder word instead. This is called a euphemism. «That bleeping dog won't stop barking!» The speaker is cross, but bleeping is not a rude word. It stands in for a swear word.
explain: Why bleeping? On TV, a short beep sound covers up swear words, so bleeping now often means "that rude word I'm not saying". Context helps you spot this: if someone is annoyed and says bleeping, they are probably cross, not talking about a sound.
explain: The word also has a literal meaning. «The microwave kept bleeping when the popcorn was ready.» Here bleeping means making short, high sounds, like a machine. Ask yourself: is this about a sound, or about feeling cross? The sentence tells you which.
fact: Bleeping means making short, high sounds, like a machine.
fact: As a euphemism, bleeping is a milder word used instead of a swear word.
fact: The bleep is the beep sound that covers swear words on TV.
fact: Bleep, bleeps, bleeped and bleeping are forms of the same verb.
fact: A euphemism is a softer word used in place of a rude or upsetting one.
exercise: «The microwave kept bleeping when the popcorn was ready.» What does bleeping mean here? | *Making short, high sounds, like a machine | Covering something up with a rude word | Cooking very slowly | Shouting very loudly
exercise: «That bleeping dog won't stop barking!» Why might the speaker say bleeping? | Because the dog is making a machine sound | *Because they are cross and do not want to say a rude word | Because the dog is very small | Because they are laughing at the dog
exercise: Find one word in this sentence that is a form of bleep. «The clock bleeps every hour.» | every | *bleeps | hour | clock
test: What is the bleep sound on TV for? | *Covering up swear words | Playing music | Making the film longer | Calling the dog home
test: «The lift bleeped as the doors closed.» What does bleeped mean here? | Opened slowly | Shouted loudly | *Made a short, high sound | Said a rude word
exam: Which word is a euphemism, a milder stand-in for a rude word? | *Bleeping | Angry | Cross | Loud
